  "query_preview": "..\n(Monday through Thursday)\nIssued at 225 AM CDT Fri Oct 2 2026\n\nAbove-normal temperature and dry conditions are expected for the \nweek ahead as the westerlies retreat to the north with a return to\nsoutherly winds. The temperature spread among bias-corrected \nprobabilistic guidance is minimal with even the 10th percentile \nindicating above-normal temperatures from mid week and beyond. \nDeterministic and ensemble guidance indicate the potential for an \nelongated mid-level ridge being the dominant influence on our \nweather. High temperatures by the end of next week could be back \nnear 90 deg F, which is ~15 deg F above-normal. The good news is \nwith the lower sun angle, shorter days, and lower dew points, \novernight temperatures will be comfortable (in the 50s and 60s deg\nF) next week.\n\nMahale",
